    {
      "url": "https://www.berwickmaine.gov/articles_T47_R821.php",
      "text": "Elections  Berwick Voters: Ask Your Questions Monday at Candidates\u2019 Night [LIVE-STREAM LINK]  For this year\u2019s Select Board Candidates' Night, Berwick residents are being encouraged to do something a little different: come to the room and take part.  On Monday, May 4 at 6pm, all five candidates for Select Board Member, Assessor, and Overseer of the Poor will gather in the Burgess Meeting Room at Town Hall for a moderated public forum led by Geoffrey Day, who regularly moderates Berwick Communications & Media events. Two seats are available for three-year terms."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.berwickmaine.gov/articles_T47_R776.php",
      "text": "Elections  Thoughtful About Berwick\u2019s Future? This Is Your Moment\u00a0\u2022 Select Board Papers Available Feb. 26  Two seats on the Berwick Select Board will be on the ballot this year, and nomination papers become available beginning February 26. According to Town Manager Arthur Capello, anyone interested in running can pick up papers from the Town Clerk starting that day. Candidates must gather at least 25 and no more than 100 signatures from registered Berwick voters."
